Sweep design
------------
Stage A — 9 plog2 ≥ 7 screenshots × 20 (IDENTITY, DCT2X2) tuples × 3
distances {0.5, 1.0, 2.0} = 540 measurements.

Lift grids (narrower than W23-2; AFV + DCT4X8 pinned at W22-1 lifts):
  IDENTITY ∈ {1.10, 1.15, 1.20, 1.25, 1.30}
  DCT2X2   ∈ {1.04, 1.07, 1.10, 1.13}
  AFV PINNED  = 0.95  (W22-1)
  DCT4X8 PINNED = 0.98 (W22-1)

Image list (windows95 DROPPED — plog2=4 < 7, handled by W35-1
classifier hint suppression `Some(false)`):
  codec_wiki   plog2=10
  gmessages    plog2=9
  graph        plog2=8
  gui          plog2=8
  imac_dark    plog2=12
  imac_g3      plog2=11
  imessage     plog2=9
  terminal     plog2=9
  windows      plog2=11

Stage B — 5 CID22-512 photos × 1 tuple (default IDENT=1.10
DCT2X2=1.04 — lowest cell) × 3 distances = 15 measurements.

NOTE on Stage B interpretation: photo encodes route through
`LossyInternalParams::entropy_mul_table` (a direct override that
ignores the production `median(mask1x1) > 95` discriminator). So
Stage B measures the SAME lifted table applied UNCONDITIONALLY to
photos — it is NOT a test of the production gate's photo-skip
behavior. The production gate's photo-skip path is verified
separately by the W22-1 `test_default_off_byte_identical` hash-lock
fixtures (36 / 36 pass on parent commit `3541912b`); see
`test_entropy_mul_table_screenshot_suppressed_values` in
`effort.rs`. Stage B remains useful as a sanity that even the
lowest cell does NOT regress photo butteraugli — it does not.

Acceptance gates
----------------
1. avg screen-class bytes Δ ≤ -0.30 %
2. no cell |bfly Δ| > 3 %
3. ≥ 80 % of cells |bfly Δ| ≤ 2 %

