Photo bit-identity (production gate path)
------------------------------------------
The W35-1 hash-lock fixtures (36 / 36 pass at parent commit
`3541912b`) verify that `with_content_aware_entropy_mul(false)`
— the default — keeps every photo encode byte-identical. No new
default-on table flip occurs in this chunk; the
`EntropyMulTable::screenshot_suppressed()` values are UNCHANGED
from W22-1. Therefore:

  - Default config: byte-identical to parent (hash-lock proven).
  - `with_content_aware_entropy_mul(true)` opt-in: same lift
    behavior as W22-1 / W35-1.
  - `with_screenshot_lift_hint(Some(true|false))` override: same
    behavior as W35-1.
  - `LossyInternalParams::entropy_mul_table = Some(...)`: still
    bypasses both gates (used by this bench; not the production
    path).

No production wiring changed in this chunk.
